## Residual risk

The post-change full `bunx nx run music-core:test --skip-nx-cache` run exposed an existing concurrent-managed-caller race: one follower observed `occupied` while another generation was starting, so the command exited 1 at `20 concurrent managed callers converge on one selected graph`. The focused client suite passes, but the full core test gate is not green. The failed test left its test daemon running; I terminated that owned daemon with SIGTERM and confirmed socket/marker cleanup. This needs a further narrow rework before approval.
